 On macOS, `pane.send_input` (used by `pane run`) and `agent.start` check the terminal's current canonical input limit before accepting a command into the input queue. An oversized encoded line, including Enter, is rejected in full; wait for the shell prompt and retry. Multiple short lines and raw-mode input remain supported. Successful responses still acknowledge queue admission, not command execution. This check covers the current submission only: it cannot inspect an earlier incomplete line or guarantee the terminal mode will remain unchanged while input is queued.
